      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "By expressing $\\operatorname{log}⁡\\sqrt{6x}$ in the form $p\\operatorname{log}⁡(6x),$ determine the value of $p.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({c}^{m})=m\\operatorname{log}⁡(c)\n$$\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡\\sqrt{6x} & =\\operatorname{log}⁡((6x)^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{log}⁡(6x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
